# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AUDIT-2026-08-11 D-21 / D-9 — numerical inputs to the headline results.
#
# The blanket `*.npy` above excluded EVERY numerical input to the force and
# transport results while the submitted manuscript's Data-and-Code-Availability
# statement asserted that "all simulation data and scripts are available".
# Measured 2026-08-17: 34 .npy under research/, 0 of them tracked.
# The un-ignores below put 31 of the 34 in the repo (see the three exclusions
# noted at the bottom of this block).
#
# MEASURED ON DISK 2026-08-17 (`find research -name '*.npy' -printf '%s\t%p\n'`),
# not estimated:
#   theta_*.npy             14 files    118,240 B
#   transport_*.npy          8 files    196,928 B
#   boundary_density_*.npy   4 files     77,952 B
#   *_dims.npy               4 files      1,152 B
#   builds/target_Cr_8site    1 file         160 B
#   ------------------------------------------------
#   TOTAL                   31 files    394,432 B  (385 KB) — no Git-LFS needed.
#
# (The audit stated "24 files, 432 KB" for theta_*/transport_*/boundary_density_*.
#  The measurement above supersedes it: theta_* is 14 files, not 12, and those
#  three globs total 393,120 B — so the audit's count was 2 low and its byte
#  total was high. The remaining 5 files (*_dims, target_Cr_8site, 1,312 B) are
#  additions of ours; the audit did not list them. Same conclusion either way:
#  this is a few hundred KB and belongs in git.)
#
# NOT covered by these globs: gs_24q_exact.npy (below) and the 2 hb_lam3_*.npy
# inside the vendored MERAKit tree (handled at the bottom of this file).
!research/data/simulations/theta_*.npy
!research/data/simulations/transport_*.npy
!research/data/simulations/boundary_density_*.npy
!research/data/simulations/*_dims.npy
!research/data/builds/target_Cr_8site.npy

# STAYS IGNORED — the one large array. gs_24q_exact.npy = 134,217,856 B
# (128 MB, 2^24 x float64), the cached 24-qubit exact ground state feeding the
# alpha measurement. Git is the wrong home for it. It belongs on ZENODO, as a
# file in the reproducibility deposit described in
# research/data/audit/MANIFEST-plan.md; it is regenerable in ~1,228 s of eigsh
# by the tracked driver interaction_energy_24q.py, so the deposit is a
# convenience, not the sole copy. Re-asserted explicitly so that a future
# broadening of the theta_*/transport_* globs above cannot pull it in.
research/data/simulations/gs_*.npy

