# external MERAKit.jl clone (keep RUN-MERAKIT.md + our pinned Project.toml/setup tracked separately)
# Provenance (upstream URL, pinned revision, license, patches): research/tools/merakit-setup/RUN-MERAKIT.md
#
# AUDIT-2026-08-11 D-21 asks that our own artifacts inside this tree be tracked:
# Manifest.toml (14,148 B — the ONLY resolved Julia dependency manifest anywhere
# in the project; D-21 measured "dependency versions 0/73"), 7 run logs
# (26,601 B) and 2 hb_lam3_*.npy operator arrays (131,328 B) = 172,077 B.
#
# THAT CANNOT BE DONE WITH `!` EXCEPTIONS HERE. Tried and measured 2026-08-17:
# rewriting this rule as `research/tools/MERAKit.jl/*` plus three negations makes
# `git check-ignore` report the paths as trackable, but they STILL cannot be
# staged — the tree holds its own `.git` (a plain clone of mhauru/MERAKit.jl at
# ace2f92, no .gitmodules), and git refuses to descend into an embedded
# repository: `git add -n` and `git add -nf` on those paths staged nothing and
# `git status -uall` collapsed the whole tree to one entry. Worse, the `/*` form
# made `git add -A` want to add MERAKit.jl as an embedded-repo GITLINK — a real
# hazard while staging the D-9/D-25 freeze commit. So the bare-directory rule
# below is kept deliberately; it is the safe form, not an oversight.
#
# The two ways to actually get those 10 artifacts into the repo — neither of
# which needs an edit to this file — are recorded in
# research/tools/merakit-setup/RUN-MERAKIT.md and
# research/data/audit/MANIFEST-plan.md §7.1:
#   (A) preferred — copy them into the already-tracked mirror
#       research/tools/merakit-setup/ (the convention CLAUDE.md already mandates
#       for the qw_*.jl drivers); or
#   (B) move research/tools/MERAKit.jl/.git out of the tree, which is now safe
#       because the upstream URL and pinned revision are recorded in
#       RUN-MERAKIT.md rather than only in the clone's own history.
research/tools/MERAKit.jl/

research/tools/juliahome/
# vendored yijian-physics/puMPS (NO upstream license -> never commit/redistribute; see pumps-setup/VENDOR.md)
research/tools/puMPS/

